# This file ensures the public/ directory is tracked by git.
# Git does not track empty directories, but the frontend Dockerfile does
# `COPY public/ ./public/`, which requires the directory to exist in the
# Docker build context.
#
# Without this (or some other file), `docker compose --profile prod build`
# (or any build with context=./frontend) will fail on fresh clones with:
#   COPY public/ ./public/
#   failed to calculate checksum of ref ...: "/public": not found
#
# You can safely delete this file once you add real static assets
# (favicon.ico, images, robots.txt, etc.) to this directory.
